). While the cursor later moves to highlight \'gayvee.eth\' in the To column, the immediate action after hand lowering shows the cursor positioned over \'78.88\'. Among the answer choices, D is the most accurate as it references the cursor being on \'78.88\'.",\n    "answer_criteria": [\n        "Mouse cursor is visible hovering over the number \'78.88\' in the Price column of the transaction table",\n        "This cursor position occurs in the timeframe immediately following the man lowering his right hand (frames 0210-0214)"\n    ]\n}'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': '📋 CRITIC FEEDBACK (Confidence: 50%)'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '{\n    "tool": "VLM_QUERY",\n    "frames": ["frames/frame_0200.jpg", "frames/frame_0201.jpg", "frames/frame_0202.jpg", "frames/frame_0203.jpg", "frames/frame_0204.jpg", "frames/frame_0205.jpg", "frames/frame_0206.jpg", "frames/frame_0207.jpg", "frames/frame_0208.jpg", "frames/frame_0209.jpg", "frames/frame_0210.jpg", "frames/frame_0211.jpg", "frames/frame_0212.jpg", "frames/frame_0213.jpg", "frames/frame_0214.jpg", "frames/frame_0215.jpg", "frames/frame_0216.jpg", "frames/frame_0217.jpg", "frames/frame_0218.jpg", "frames/frame_0219.jpg", "frames/frame_0220.jpg"],\n    "prompt": "Based on these frames (including context before/after), verify if the answer \'3\' (which corresponds to choice C: The mouse cursor slid to the number \'0.9\' and painted over it) is correct for the question. First, check if all question criteria are met: 1) Website background with supermarket icon visible, 2) Website background with shopping cart icon visible, 3) Labels for price and source keywords visible on screen, 4) Man wearing sunglasses visible on screen, 5) Man talking into a microphone visible, 6) Man\'s right hand in a lowered position. Then, specifically observe what happens on the screen after the man lowers his right hand - does the mouse cursor move to \'0.9\' and paint over it? Pay close attention to temporal sequence and cursor movements